From 993fd28e3ad976a23def2aa744cbaa538e661219 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fi3 <you@example.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 11:17:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] ADD backend command execution so selected-agent slash
 inputs bypass prompt sends

Route selected-agent slash-prefixed input through a provider-neutral backend command hook instead of the ordinary prompt send path. This lets backends such as Codex execute exposed app-server commands like /status and /fork against the active session while frontends and controllers keep the raw slash input visible in the selected chat.
---
 docs/architecture.md  |   8 +++
 src/agent_runtime.rs  |  14 +++++
 src/cli.rs            |  75 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/codex.rs          | 117 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------------
 tests/terminal_app.rs |  40 +++++++++++++--
 tests/workspace.rs    |  49 ++++++++++++++----
 6 files changed, 248 insertions(+), 55 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/architecture.md b/docs/architecture.md
index 1c5bdc9..88cc239 100644
--- a/docs/architecture.md
+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -163,8 +163,13 @@ rather than using `@work-leaf` read, patch, or lock directives.
 
 - `AgentBackend::launch` starts an agent session from an `AgentLaunch`.
 - `AgentBackend::send` sends a prompt to an existing agent session.
+- `AgentBackend::command` executes a selected-agent slash command against an existing backend
+  session without passing the command through ordinary prompt injection or Work Leaf command parsing.
 - `AgentBackend::launch_streaming` and `AgentBackend::send_streaming` provide real-time output to a
   sink of `AgentStreamEvent` values. Their default implementations call the non-streaming methods.
+- `AgentBackend::command_streaming` provides the streaming form of selected-agent slash command
+  execution. Its default implementation calls `command`, so providers that do not expose a separate
+  command protocol keep a small implementation surface.
 - `AgentBackend::launch_streaming_interruptible` and
   `AgentBackend::send_streaming_interruptible` extend the streaming calls with a provider-neutral
   stop detector. Providers that can interrupt an in-flight turn use the detector to stop generation
@@ -297,6 +302,9 @@ The primary public methods are:
   `launch_prepared_agent_streaming_with_ids` for UI-driven launch flows.
 - `CommandChat::send_to_agent`, `send_to_agent_streaming`, and
   `send_to_agent_streaming_with_ids` for UI-driven message flows.
+- `CommandChat::execute_agent_command`, `execute_agent_command_streaming`, and
+  `execute_agent_command_streaming_with_ids` for selected-agent slash commands that must be handled
+  by the active backend session instead of the ordinary prompt path.
 - `CommandChat::shutdown_agents` and `shutdown_handle` for lifecycle cleanup.
 
 `CommandChat` uses the active `AgentProfile` when launching user agents, reviewers, and linearizers.
